<http://data.silknow.org/object/675d8cd0-d42f-376e-af6a-c45b1b7cdfc1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A double-tiered circular work table, raised on a tripod support, the top tier set with a Sèvres porcelain plaque decorated with sprigs of flowers, the lower tier set with marquetry of scrolls.  The table is veneered with tulipwood and other woods on a carcase of oak, the drawers lined with velvet and watered silk and edged with braid; drawer fittings of gilt-bronze and castors of lignum vitae."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/675d8cd0-d42f-376e-af6a-c45b1b7cdfc1> .

